from pathlib import Path
import json,hashlib
B=Path(__file__).parent
entries=[]
def add(q,a,refs):
 entries.append({'id':f'Q{len(entries)+1:02}','question':q,'answer':a,'source_refs':refs})
add('For two Spirits, how are the Fear pool/deck and Invader deck prepared, what initial Blight pool is used with and without a Blight Card, and what final Invader action completes setup?', 'Use 8 Fear markers, 9 shuffled Fear cards divided 3/3/3 by Terror II and III dividers; Invader deck is 3 Stage I above 4 Stage II above 5 Stage III, randomized within each stage with one unused card per stage removed unseen. Initial Blight is 5 with a Healthy Island card (2 per player +1), or 11 without (5 per player +1). Setup Explore the top card normally and leave it face-up in Build; Ravage is initially empty.', ['CORE p.6; p.4 board','FAQ Setup: one-more-blight-errata'])
add('A Spirit chooses Growth with two Add Presence actions. May the second placement use the first as its range origin? Which Presence-track disks may be taken, and how do uncovered Energy/Card Plays numbers combine?', 'Yes; resolve Growth actions in chosen order, so the first placement can extend the second. Each placement takes the leftmost remaining Presence from either chosen track. Use only the highest uncovered Energy number and highest uncovered Card Plays number, not their sum.', ['CORE pp.8,14','FAQ Core: .7w4g8p3'])
add('A Spirit has no Presence on its tracks but has Presence on the island and some destroyed disks. How can an Add Presence instruction be resolved, where is range measured, and can destroyed disks be used?', 'Reposition one of its island Presence instead of taking a track disk. First choose a legal destination measured from existing island Presence, including the disk about to be repositioned, then take any of its island disks. Destroyed Presence is unavailable unless explicitly allowed.', ['CORE p.14 sidebar','FAQ Core: .bu6od08; .7w4g8oc'])
add('When are Fast and Slow Power Cards paid for and their Elements gained? Can promised Fast-phase Energy pay for the Spirit-phase cards, and do unspent Energy or unused Card Plays carry over?', 'Play and pay for all cards in the Spirit Phase, gaining their Elements immediately, including Slow cards. Later Fast-phase Energy cannot pay these earlier costs. Unspent Energy carries over; unused Card Plays do not.', ['CORE pp.8,13,16','FAQ Core: .7w4g8qz'])
add('May a Fast Power wait until Slow, may Powers interrupt each other, and when must a Slow Power’s target be selected?', 'A Fast Power must be used during Fast or foregone; it cannot wait until Slow. Players choose Power order but finish one before another. Choose the Slow target when using the Power in Slow, using the then-current legal range and target, not irrevocably at card play.', ['CORE pp.8,10','FAQ Core: .9v5ka9d'])
add('In a Ravage a land has one Town, one Explorer and two undamaged Dahan, with no Defend or prior Blight. Resolve damage to land, Dahan, surviving counterattack and resulting Fear if the players destroy the Town.', 'Invaders do 3 Damage simultaneously to land and Dahan, adding one Blight, killing one Dahan and damaging the other by 1. The surviving Dahan still deals 2 Damage, destroying the Town and generating 1 Fear. Dahan do not absorb/prevent land damage; partial Dahan damage clears at Time Passes.', ['CORE pp.9,11,15-16'])
add('Compare a Ravage reduced to zero Damage by Defend with a Ravage skipped entirely. Do Dahan fight back in each, and does Spirit Presence counterattack?', 'Surviving Dahan counterattack for 2 each even if Defend reduces Invader damage to zero. If the Ravage is skipped entirely, no counterattack. Presence does not counterattack.', ['CORE p.9'])
add('During Build, what is added to lands containing only Explorers, equal numbers of Towns and Cities, more Towns than Cities, or no Invaders? Are Towns upgraded?', 'Only Explorers or equal Town/City numbers: add one Town. More Towns than Cities: add one City. No Invaders: no Build. These are new pieces from supply; no Town is removed/upgraded.', ['CORE p.10'])
add('Which matching lands Explore, how many Explorers are added if there are multiple sources, do Explorers themselves provide a source, and what happens if no Invader Card can be drawn?', 'Explore matching lands that contain a Town/City or are adjacent to a Town/City/Ocean. Add exactly one Explorer from supply regardless of sources or existing pieces. Explorers are not sources. Needing to draw when the deck is empty loses; drawing the last existing card alone does not.', ['CORE pp.10,12,15'])
add('After Explore, where do the Invader cards go? How are a Stage III two-terrain card and a Stage II flag handled without an Adversary?', 'Discard old Ravage, move Build to Ravage and just-explored card to Build. Stage III acts in both terrain types subject to usual action restrictions. Ignore Stage II flags without an Adversary.', ['CORE p.10'])
add('In a two-Spirit game with 7 of 8 Fear markers already generated, an effect generates 3 Fear and earning a card exposes Terror II. Explain marker handling, new Terror timing, and when the card is revealed/resolved.', 'Move the eighth marker to earn the top Fear card face-down, reset all 8 to the pool and put the remaining 2 generated Fear toward the next card. Terror II applies as soon as exposed (subject to outcome check at action-tree end). Keep card hidden until Fear step, resolving in earned order at the then-current Terror level only.', ['CORE pp.9,12','FAQ Core: .3y28aut; .9v5kfq7'])
add('A Fear card resolved in the Fear step earns another Fear card and exposes a higher Terror Level. When is that new card resolved, at which level do subsequent cards resolve, and do “each player” choices require that player’s own Presence?', 'Put the new card at the bottom of the resolving stack and resolve it in this same Fear step. Subsequent cards use the new Terror Level only. Each player resolves their instructions completely, restricted only by the card; own Presence/range is not required. Generic Presence/Sacred Site conditions may use any Spirit’s unless specifically individualized.', ['CORE pp.9,12','FAQ Core: .3y28aus; fear-cards-checking-for-presence'])
add('A land with existing Blight has two Presence from Spirit A and one from Spirit B. One new Blight is added after setup. Describe Presence losses, cascade choices and what happens if the cascade enters another already-Blighted land.', 'Destroy one Presence each of A and B, putting destroyed disks beside the island, not on tracks. Add the original Blight and cascade one additional Blight to one adjacent land, not all. If that land already has Blight it too loses one Presence per Spirit there and cascades again. Existing amount of Blight does not multiply the one cascade.', ['CORE pp.9,15'])
add('Where does setup Blight come from versus Blight added during play? When a Healthy card empties how is its new pool obtained, does the setup +1 repeat, and can removing Blight make it Healthy again?', 'Setup island Blight comes from the box, not initial pool, and does not cascade or destroy Presence. Play Blight comes from card/board pool. When Healthy empties flip and follow the Blighted instructions, adding the printed new per-player pool from box; do not apply setup +1 again. Removed island Blight returns to currently face-up card/board pool; a Blighted card never flips back.', ['CORE pp.6,15,18','FAQ Setup: .9v5ka5b; one-more-blight-errata','FAQ Core: .7w4g8r7'])
add('Explain how Elements apply to multiple thresholds and multiple Powers. May an innate be used twice with twice the Elements, may its levels use different lands, and how does an “Instead” level work?', 'Elements are checked, not spent, so may meet any number of Powers/thresholds. An innate is normally one use, regardless of surplus Elements. Use all met levels top to bottom on one target, with Instead replacing previous effects. May pretend to have fewer Elements for the entire Power, not cherry-pick levels.', ['CORE pp.14,16-17','FAQ Core: .bu6od0c'])
add('A legal target lacks pieces needed for one printed instruction. May the Power still be used? May the player choose individual unwanted instructions to skip, or forego the whole Power and recover its Energy?', 'May use it; perform instructions in order, skipping impossible parts and doing the rest. Cannot skip possible mandatory instructions at will (apart from permitted choices, up-to, or selecting fewer Elements consistently). May forego the whole Power; no Energy refund, and played-card Elements remain while in play.', ['CORE pp.16-17'])
add('Explain gaining a new Minor or Major Power, including how many are drawn, where kept/unkept cards go, Major Forgetting options and the consequences of Forgetting a card already in play.', 'Choose Minor or Major, draw 4 from that deck, reshuffling its discard if needed; keep one in hand, discard the other three to its deck discard. Gaining a Major requires Forgetting any one owned card (hand, personal discard, in play, even new Major); forgotten Minor/Major goes to its deck discard, Unique under panel. Forgetting in-play immediately loses Elements and unused use; previously resolved effects persist for their normal duration.', ['CORE p.18'])
add('How do Damage, Destroy, Remove and Replace differ for Fear and survival? Can Damage from separate normal Powers combine, does Damage normally hurt Dahan, and does replacement erase prior Damage?', 'Damage normally means to Invaders only, distributed as chosen in target land; can combine within turn, immediately destroying pieces at Damage >= Health. Destroying Town/City produces 1/2 Fear in addition to explicit Fear. Remove/Replace generate none automatically; Replace retains prior Damage and may cause destruction if Damage meets new Health (then destruction Fear applies). Surviving Damage clears at Time Passes. Dahan are harmed by Powers only if explicitly stated.', ['CORE pp.15-16,18','FAQ Core: .bu6oczl'])
add('Does increased Power Range extend Gather/Push distance, may multiple pieces come from/go to different adjacent lands, may pieces go into the Ocean normally, and may “up to” be zero?', 'Range boost changes reaching the target, not Gather/Push adjacency. Gather from adjacent land(s) into target; Push from target to adjacent land(s), distributing among them freely. No ordinary Ocean/off-board Push, as Ocean is not a land (specific Spirit exceptions override). Up to may be zero.', ['CORE pp.13,19,31'])
add('State all four Terror victory conditions, the three standard defeat routes, and the result when a single Ravage loses a Spirit’s last Presence but surviving Dahan remove the final required Invader. Do you finish other lands first?', 'Terror I: no Invaders; II: no Towns/Cities; III: no Cities; earning final Fear card reveals Victory and wins without resolving it. Defeat: exhausted Blight pool as instructed (or board pool empty), any Spirit without island Presence, or need to draw Invader card from empty deck. Complete current action plus triggered actions before outcome check; single-land Ravage can yield sacrifice victory if both win/loss met. Do not continue to other land Ravages before that check.', ['CORE p.12','FAQ Core: .7w4gcs0; .bu6oc8v; .9v5kfq7'])
q={'game':'Spirit Island','scope':'Original base game standard core + applicable linked Living FAQ; optional modules excluded','benchmark_version':'seed-v1','questions':[{'id':e['id'],'question':e['question']} for e in entries]}
k={'game':'Spirit Island','benchmark_version':'seed-v1','grading':'Correct only if every requested material fact resolved, no contradiction or unsupported guess. Partial for missing/unresolved parts, incorrect for any material contradiction. Judge content rather than support label.','answers':[{'id':e['id'],'answer':e['answer'],'source_refs':e['source_refs']} for e in entries]}
d=B/'seed-v1'; d.mkdir(exist_ok=True)
for name,v in [('questions.json',q),('answer-key.json',k)]:
 p=d/name
 if p.exists(): raise RuntimeError(f'Refusing overwrite: {p}')
 p.write_text(json.dumps(v,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)+'\n')
(d/'question-bank.md').write_text('# Spirit Island seed bank v1\n\nPrepared source-first before any canonical summary existed. Fixed before readers.\n\n'+'\n\n'.join(f"## {e['id']}\n\n{e['question']}\n\n**Expected:** {e['answer']}\n\n**Sources:** {'; '.join(e['source_refs'])}" for e in entries)+'\n')
(d/'input-manifest.json').write_text(json.dumps({'question_count':len(entries),'sha256':{str(p):hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest() for p in [d/'questions.json',d/'answer-key.json']},'source_manifest':'../source-manifest.json','summary_existed_at_bank_creation':False},indent=2)+'\n')
p=json.loads((B/'progress.json').read_text());p.update(phase='summary-drafting',question_count=len(entries));(B/'progress.json').write_text(json.dumps(p,indent=2)+'\n')
print('Frozen',len(entries),'seed questions.')
